            (with an eye towards
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} (infinity,1)-toposes
            %strong equifibered natural transformations
            and is considered in
          %ul
            %li#Rezk10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
                , p. 9 of
                %em Toposes and homotopy toposes
                (2010) (
                %a{:href => "https://rezk.web.illinois.edu/homotopy-topos-sketch.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Rezk14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
                , p. 2 of
                %em When are homotopy colimits compatible with homotopy base change?
                (2014) (
                %a{:href => "https://rezk.web.illinois.edu/i-hate-the-pi-star-kan-condition.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The name “equifibered” comes from the fact that since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_x
            is a pullback of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected
            %em all
            components of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            have isomorphic fibers.)
